# Line endings, pinned as a property of the asset — not left to a per-machine
# `core.autocrlf`, which is invisible to the repo and to every future clone.
#
# This repo has a remote and is cloned on unknown platforms, so the DEFAULT is
# plain `text=auto`: git stores LF and each checkout gets its platform's
# ending. Only the exceptions below pin a specific ending, and each one names
# the property that breaks without it.

* text=auto

# --- Receipt-stable regeneration assets ----------------------------------
# archdiag emits html whose sha256 IS the deliverable's freeze receipt (B-3 in
# the skill). Multi-line template literals inherit the SOURCE file's endings,
# so a CRLF checkout of the library would push \r\n into every emitted file and
# change every receipt with no content change behind it. Writer (node, LF) and
# checkout must agree. The source environment pins the same paths for the same
# reason; shipping the library without the pin would ship an asset whose stated
# invariant this repo breaks. `index.mjs` additionally normalizes \r\n at
# emission, so a receipt survives even a CRLF-editing tool touching a source.
architecture-diagramming/archdiag/**            text eol=lf
# The build script and its emitted page are pinned for the same reason, one
# level up: a multi-line template literal inherits ITS OWN file's endings, and
# the emitted html must stay byte-equal on disk to what build() wrote or its
# receipt is no longer comparable in place. (index.mjs also normalizes \r\n at
# emission — belt and braces, same property, and neither alone is enough: the
# normalizer protects the OUTPUT, this line protects the working-tree copy.)
architecture-diagramming/*.build.mjs            text eol=lf
architecture-diagramming/*.html                 text eol=lf

# --- Files a POSIX loader reads directly ---------------------------------
# A CR inside a shebang makes the kernel look for an interpreter literally
# named "bash\r".
*.sh    text eol=lf

# --- Windows-native scripts: stated, not inherited ------------------------
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf
*.ps1   text eol=crlf

# --- Binary safety net ----------------------------------------------------
# None tracked today. Listed in advance because the damage from normalizing a
# binary is silent corruption, and the moment one is added is the moment
# nobody is thinking about this file.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
